{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Behind the way of the going down of the sun, behind</b> the crossing of the Jordan in <b>the way of the going down the sun.</b> That which Rashi explained — far and onward to a distance — is not very far, but rather sixty mil from the Jordan, and on that very day when they crossed the Jordan, after they performed the commandments incumbent upon them at Mount Gerizim and Mount Ebal, they came and camped at Gilgal, as is explicit in Joshua and in tractate Sotah." "<b>Opposite Gilgal.</b> It tells you at which point along the mountains, since the mountains are long."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The text reads פירש״י which appears to be a reverent abbreviation of 'Rashi interpreted' (פירש ר״י); rendered accordingly, consistent with the compiler's practice of drawing from Rashi without naming sources."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:30.093146751Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}